        "Present perfect (have / has + past participle): a past action that matters now, or an experience. \"I have finished my work.\" \"She has visited Delhi twice.\"": "المضارع التام (present perfect): have / has + التصريف الثالث للفعل (past participle). يُستعمل لفعل حدث في الماضي وما زال مهمًا الآن، أو لتجربة مررت بها. \"I have finished my work.\" \"She has visited Delhi twice.\"",
        "It is often used with already, yet, just, ever, never, since and for.": "يُستعمل غالبًا مع already و yet و just و ever و never و since و for.",
        "Use the simple past, not the present perfect, with a finished time: \"I finished my work at 5 p.m.\" — not \"I have finished at 5 p.m.\"": "مع وقت انتهى، استعمل الماضي البسيط لا المضارع التام: \"I finished my work at 5 p.m.\" — وليس \"I have finished at 5 p.m.\"",
        "Past perfect (had + past participle): an action finished before another past action. \"When we reached the hall, the film had started.\"": "الماضي التام (past perfect): had + التصريف الثالث. يُستعمل لفعل انتهى قبل فعل آخر في الماضي. \"When we reached the hall, the film had started.\"",
        "Present perfect continuous (have / has been + verb-ing): an action that started in the past and is still going on. \"I have been studying for two hours.\"": "المضارع التام المستمر (present perfect continuous): have / has been + verb-ing. يُستعمل لفعل بدأ في الماضي وما زال مستمرًا. \"I have been studying for two hours.\"",
